{"name":"Strawberry, Basil & Black Pepper Ice Cream","permalink":"strawberry-basil-ice-cream","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/StrawberryBasilIceCream.scala","source":"Kit","description":null,"tagline":null,"notes":["I tend to double up this recipe to make enough for a few days.\n\nYou can use up the egg whites by making <a href=\"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/easy-chocolate-mousse\" rel=\"nofollow\">chocolate mousse</a>.","I vibed the quantity of pepper. A few grinder twists wasn't enough so I added a healthy dose the second time. If I make this again I'll measure it in tsp. Consider using a fine spice mill or grinding with a mortar and pestal, because my supermarket grinder left large pieces.","There was only 1/4tsp of vanilla essence left the first time I made this. I think 1/2-1tsp would work best.","While the food colouring is optional the mixture is a concrete grey by default, so I'd recommend it! I've doubled the quantity of food colouring when writing this up because the mixture was still a bit grey, but YMMV.","Stephani tasting notes: Interesting and complex. Most liked so far. Strong basil flavour with moments of strawberry and black pepper.","Kit tasting notes: smells like pesto, tastes juicy and fruity with strawberry dominating the basil. Pepper a bit weak. Might improve after a few days in the freezer but I should consider soaking the pepper in the mascarpone for a day in the fridge before making ice cream. Consider adding a dash of lime juice to balance the strawberry sweetness, like <a href=\"https://peterleymanorfarm.co.uk/strawberry-basil-and-black-pepper-ice-cream/\">this recipe</a> does."],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Pudding"],"inherited_tags":[],"image":{"src":"https://i.reciba.se/strawberry-basil-ice-cream.jpg","width":1080,"height":1080},"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Strawberry powder","quantity":"12.5g","prep":null,"notes":"freeze dried, no added sugar"},{"name":"Fresh Basil","quantity":"15g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Black pepper","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Green Food Colouring","quantity":"1tsp","prep":null,"notes":"optional"},{"name":"Mascarpone","quantity":"230g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Eggs","quantity":"2","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Icing Sugar","quantity":"60g","prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Carefully separate the egg yolks using your hands or spoons. Put aside the egg whites for another recipe.","Whisk the egg yolks and sugar in a bowl, with an electric mixer, until thick and light in colour.","Separate the basil leaves from their stems and put in a blender alongside a dollop of the mascarpone. Puree with a food blender.","Add the basil puree and the remaining mascarpone to the whisked egg yolks. Grind in a large dose of black pepper.","Mix in the strawberry powder enough that it won't spray everywhere, then whisk all the ingredients together.","Decant into a freezer suitable dish and freeze for at least 6 hours."]}